From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:48:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harness): hand framework text notices to codex-native
 and pi-native

Framework notice blocks are how the server and runner give the model
context with a message that must never become the user's text; today they
only carry the downscaled-image notice. A feature that wants to tell the
agent something at the start of its next turn (without starting one) has
no channel for plain text, and codex-native and pi-native read only the
image form.

- A notice block may now carry framework-owned "text"
  (framework_text_notice_block); framework_notices returns it beside the
  upload notices, so Claude SDK (UserPromptSubmit hook context), the
  OpenAI Agents SDK and other harnesses that expand notices (system
  messages), and claude-native (its framework-context prompt hook) get it
  unchanged.
- codex-native stages a message's text notices in the bridge directory,
  and a new framework-context UserPromptSubmit hook hands them to Codex
  as additionalContext, once. The shell answers alone while no notice
  waits, so a prompt pays no interpreter start; the subcommand lives in
  the policy-hook module, so the existing trust handshake covers it.
- pi-native passes them on the inbox payload; the extension adds them as
  a hidden custom message from before_agent_start, once.
- The runner's executor adapter joined the "text" of every block when it
  flattened a message for an executor that takes plain text, so a text
  notice became part of the user's own prompt (claude-native typed it into
  Claude Code, the SDK harnesses sent it as user text). Executors now say
  whether they read framework notices (reads_framework_notices): those get
  the blocks intact, every other one gets the message without them, and the
  text join skips notice blocks.

Not proposed upstream yet.

Docs: none (internal channel; the open items docs describe the note that uses it)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
